class:: ShiftLogicOsc
summary:: Oscillator-clocked binary register with frequency feedback
categories:: UGens>Generators>Deterministic
related:: Guides/NovelOscillators

description::

ShiftLogicOsc couples two bandlimited triangle oscillators through a fixed-size
binary shift register. Oscillator A clocks the register, oscillator B supplies
comparator data, and the oldest selected bits form a bipolar DAC value that
feeds both frequencies in octaves. Random decisions use only the
construction-time seed.

The closest vanilla building blocks are link::Classes/LFTri:: and
link::Classes/Stepper::. ShiftLogicOsc keeps oscillator phase, bit updates, DAC
conversion, and feedback in one sample-coherent server state.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: freqA
Signed base frequency of the clock oscillator in hertz.

argument:: freqB
Signed base frequency of the data oscillator in hertz.

argument:: feedbackA
Clock-frequency feedback depth in octaves, clamped to code::-8..8::.

argument:: feedbackB
Data-frequency feedback depth in octaves, clamped to code::-8..8::.

argument:: compare
Threshold compared with oscillator B.

argument:: change
Probability of shifting a new candidate bit, clamped to code::0..1::. A failed
decision rotates the existing register.

argument:: slew
Smoothing time for the fifth output in seconds. It does not affect feedback.

argument:: bits
Initialization-rate register length from code::3:: through code::32::.

argument:: dacBits
Initialization-rate count of oldest bits used by the DAC, from code::1::
through code::bits::.

argument:: mode
Initialization-rate data rule: code::0:: comparator, code::1:: comparator XOR
oldest bit, code::2:: rotate oldest bit, or code::3:: seeded random bit.

argument:: seed
Initialization-rate nonnegative deterministic seed.

argument:: mul
Multiplier applied to all five outputs.

argument:: add
Offset added to all five outputs after multiplication.

returns::
Clock oscillator, data oscillator, current least-significant bit, bipolar DAC
step, and smoothed DAC value.

method:: kr

ShiftLogicOsc is audio-rate only. This method throws an error.

subsection:: Discussion

The unsmoothed value code::q:: sets effective frequency as
code::f * 2.pow(feedback * q)::. A phase boundary clocks the same deterministic
rule for either sign of frequency. All storage is contained in the UGen.

examples::

code::
(
{ ShiftLogicOsc.ar(90, 113)[4] * 0.07 }.play;
)
::

code::
(
{
    var signal = ShiftLogicOsc.ar(
        51, 73, feedbackA: 1.1, feedbackB: -0.7,
        compare: LFNoise1.kr(0.2).range(-0.4, 0.4),
        change: 0.7, slew: 0.06,
        bits: 12, dacBits: 5, seed: 9182
    );
    Splay.ar([signal[0], signal[1], signal[4]]) * 0.045;
}.play;
)
::

